A||N||2||fropuff||Seat back.. cover removal||||1||
Z||000000||fropuff||12-12-2001||07:57 PM||||Hey guys.  I'm attempting to put on my Mr Mikes seat covers.  I have to wait until tomorrow to get a T50 torx bit anyway.  My question is..how do you remove the cover for the seat back, without damaging the cover?  On the video, he shows himself slicing through the back with a razor blade.  I don't really want to do this, as I can get $75 for the old covers.  I've seen covers for sale all the time, so I know they can come off undamaged.  Thanks for any help. ||||reg||1
Z||000001||FieroBUZZ||12-12-2001||08:13 PM||||Once you get going it is pretty obvious. Remove the hog rings as you get to them and the bars, etc. The cover will pull off. Just remember how it all goes back together. Little drawings and notes help, but maybe it's just that I'm forgetful.<BR>Gary||||reg||1
Z||000002||fropuff||12-12-2001||10:06 PM||||Thanks a lot for the help.  I found out how to do it five minutes after I posted!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  I got the old covers off the passenger seat.  Tomorrow I'll do the other seat, and this weekend, I'll put the new covers on!  I can't wait.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  By the way, hog rings suck.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
